.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-wallets - Manage the logged-in account's wallets (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 wallets [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List and manage the wallets of an account.

.PP
All wallet endpoints require a login ('rail0 auth login') — they are scoped to
your own account. When listing, --account defaults to the session account; if
given it must be your own account (the gateway rejects another account's id with
403). To discover ANOTHER merchant's accepted wallets/tokens without a session,
use 'rail0 payment-methods'. The verbs below act on one wallet (id or 0x
address) of the session account.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--account\fP=""
	Your account id to list (default: the logged-in session account; must be your own)

.PP
\fB--active\fP=""
	Filter wallets by active flag ('true' or 'false')

.PP
\fB--chain-id\fP=0
	Restrict nested tokens to this chain id

.PP
\fB--default\fP=""
	Restrict nested token holdings to the default one ('true' or 'false')

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for wallets

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Wallets per page

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort wallets (e.g. -created_at)

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--symbol\fP=""
	Restrict nested tokens to this symbol, e.g. USDC (alias: --token)

.PP
\fB--token-active\fP=""
	Restrict nested token holdings by active flag ('true' or 'false')


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 wallets                                   # session account
  rail0 wallets --account 019e748b-… --chain-id 5042002 --symbol USDC
  rail0 wallets get 0xABCD…
  rail0 wallets create --address 0xABCD…
.EE


